## F. Defend the Final Design – 2 Marks

The redesigned circular array successfully addresses the repeated-shifting limitation.

**Advantages:**

- New transactions are inserted without shifting existing elements.
- Only one array position is updated for each insertion.
- The latest 10 transactions are maintained.
- The memory requirement remains almost the same.

**Disadvantages:**

- The display logic is slightly more complicated.
- The program requires an additional index variable.
- It stores only the latest 10 transactions and does not maintain the complete transaction history.

**When the original design may be preferable:**

The original design is easier for beginners to understand and is suitable when the number of transactions is small.

**Final Conclusion:**

The circular array is a better choice when transactions are added frequently because it avoids unnecessary shifting. It achieves the redesign objective while maintaining the same storage capacity and output requirement. Therefore, I would prefer the circular array for this application.
